    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-73736",
      "knowledge_point_id": "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0",
      "knowledge_point": "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar",
      "problem": "Find $t$ given that the vectors $p=⟨t,1,t⟩$, $q=⟨2,-1,-1⟩$, and $r=⟨3,0,1⟩$ are coplanar.",
      "worked_solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}t & 1 & t \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =t\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+t\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =t((-1)\\cdot 1-0\\cdot (-1))-(2\\cdot 1-3\\cdot (-1))+t(2\\cdot 0-3\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-t-5+3t \\\\  & =2t-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ 2t-5 & =0 \\\\ 2t & =5 \\\\ t & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=\\frac{5}{2}.$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{5}{3}",
