  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052415",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-49386",
      "knowledge_point_id": "2feb2115-bd75-5c09-87cc-f10cf46c182f",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating Indefinite Integrals of Algebraic Functions Using Substitution",
      "problem": "Given that $u=x-1$, which integral is equivalent to $\\int x\\sqrt[5]{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $u=x-1,$ then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n$x=u+1.$\n\nNow we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\sqrt[5]{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (u+1)(\\sqrt[5]{u})(\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int (u+1)({u}^{1/5})(\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int ({u}^{6/5}+{u}^{1/5})\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\int ({u}^{6/5}+{u}^{1/5})\\text{d}u",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\int {u}^{1/5}\\,\\text{d}u",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\int ({u}^{6/5}-{u}^{1/5})\\text{d}u",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\int {u}^{6/5}\\,\\text{d}u",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\int ({u}^{1/5}+{u}^{-1/5})\\text{d}u",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "knowledge_point_source_id": 458,
