  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-121278",
      "knowledge_point_id": "d8033e21-86ab-5dc6-8060-a0b5c134bf9d",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying Regions Where a Function Is Positive or Negative Using a Sign Table",
      "problem": "Consider the expression $f(x,y)=(x+1)(2-y).$ What are the missing entries in the sign table of $f(x,y),$ shown below?\n\n| $y>2$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<2$ |  |  |\n|  | $x<-1$ | $x>-1$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=-1$ and $y=2.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/d5d7c89d619aa13d7fea8bc1260a08cb8678fb260e4431508c5f4c8c53e7ba5e.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/6cce64627f21f6cc17efc789614a0bd582ded827a0938f01c9b756e0cb461862.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $(x+1)$ | $(2-y)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-left | $(-2,3)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(0,3)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-2,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(0,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\n \n\nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052876/assets/c24cc3ab0812bfae6834ff8c3a68668c3925f6e39e29a453ea6bc27fbc9f6c74.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the table as follows:\n\n| $y>2$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<2$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n|  | $x<-1$ | $x>-1$ |",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "| $-$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $+$ |",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "| $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $-$ |",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "| $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "knowledge_point_source_id": 9412,
